                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A)
            may be identified with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            itself; that is, we identify
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i,a)
            for the unique index
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
          %p
            The disjoint union of the empty family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ()
            is
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty
          %h2#internal_version Internal version
          %p
            (This is internal in the sense of ‘internal direct sum’, not
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internalization
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
          %p
            If a family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_i)_{i: I}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            of a given set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are all pairwise disjoint (that is,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_i \cap A_j
            has an element only if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = j
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            and
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcup_i A_i
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} naturally bijective
            with the (external) disjoint union defined above. Conversely, given an external disjoint union
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨄
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \biguplus_i A_i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j
            may be identified with a subset of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨄
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \biguplus_i A_i
            (as explained above); these subsets are all pairwise disjoint, and their union is the entire disjoint union.
          %p
            Accordingly, a union of pairwise disjoint subsets may be called an
            = succeed "." do
              %strong internal disjoint union
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+unions+of+countable+sets+are+countable"} countable unions of countable sets are countable
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
